{"v":1,"book":"gita","n":14,"title":"Three modes (Gunas) of nature","narrator":{"name":"Brian","voice":"en-US-BrianMultilingualNeural"},"duration":278.28,"scenes":[{"layout":"title","headline":"The Three Gunas","visual":["Goodness, passion and ignorance"],"L":[],"say":"Chapter Fourteen. The Three Modes of Nature, the gunas. Three forces that shape everything we are and do.","start":0.0,"at":0.576,"end":9.0,"words":[[0.05,0.388,"Chapter"],[0.45,0.65,"Fourteen"],[1.5,0.087,"The"],[1.6,0.325,"Three"],[1.938,0.362,"Modes"],[2.312,0.125,"of"],[2.45,0.575,"Nature"],[3.05,0.113,"the"],[3.175,0.575,"gunas"],[4.15,0.338,"Three"],[4.5,0.575,"forces"],[5.088,0.175,"that"],[5.275,0.412,"shape"],[5.713,0.487,"everything"],[6.213,0.163,"we"],[6.388,0.3,"are"],[6.7,0.113,"and"],[6.825,0.362,"do"]]},{"layout":"verse","headline":"","visual":[],"L":["L1"],"ref":"14.03","verse":"My material Nature is the womb of creation wherein I place the seed of consciousness from which all beings are born, O Arjuna.","key":true,"vs":[10,33],"say":"Krishna begins with the origin of all life. Verse three. My material Nature is the womb of creation wherein I place the seed of consciousness from which all beings are born, O Arjuna.","start":9.0,"at":9.576,"end":22.968,"words":[[0.087,0.45,"Krishna"],[0.55,0.525,"begins"],[1.087,0.212,"with"],[1.312,0.062,"the"],[1.387,0.537,"origin"],[1.938,0.125,"of"],[2.075,0.212,"all"],[2.3,0.475,"life"],[3.175,0.275,"Verse"],[3.462,0.438,"three"],[4.3,0.125,"My"],[4.438,0.475,"material"],[4.925,0.475,"Nature"],[5.412,0.163,"is"],[5.588,0.1,"the"],[5.7,0.275,"womb"],[5.987,0.1,"of"],[6.1,0.562,"creation"],[6.675,0.375,"wherein"],[7.062,0.125,"I"],[7.2,0.388,"place"],[7.6,0.087,"the"],[7.7,0.312,"seed"],[8.025,0.075,"of"],[8.113,0.662,"consciousness"],[8.787,0.188,"from"],[8.988,0.188,"which"],[9.188,0.225,"all"],[9.425,0.312,"beings"],[9.75,0.15,"are"],[9.912,0.5,"born"],[10.775,0.212,"O"],[11.0,0.588,"Arjuna"]]},{"layout":"verse","headline":"","visual":[],"L":["L2"],"ref":"14.05","verse":"Sattva or goodness; Rajas or passion, activity; and Tamas or ignorance, inertia — these three modes (Ropes, Gunas) of material Nature (Prakriti) fetter the eternal individual soul to the body, O Arjuna.","key":true,"vs":[20,52],"say":"And then he names the three forces that tie the soul to the body. Notice the word ropes. Verse five. Sattva or goodness; Rajas or passion, activity; and Tamas or ignorance, inertia — these three modes (Ropes, Gunas) of material Nature (Prakriti) fetter the eternal individual soul to the body, O Arjuna.","start":22.968,"at":23.544,"end":48.504,"words":[[0.087,0.138,"And"],[0.237,0.175,"then"],[0.425,0.163,"he"],[0.6,0.438,"names"],[1.05,0.113,"the"],[1.175,0.275,"three"],[1.462,0.537,"forces"],[2.013,0.188,"that"],[2.212,0.312,"tie"],[2.538,0.087,"the"],[2.638,0.362,"soul"],[3.013,0.125,"to"],[3.15,0.087,"the"],[3.25,0.45,"body"],[4.062,0.425,"Notice"],[4.5,0.1,"the"],[4.612,0.312,"word"],[4.938,0.525,"ropes"],[5.862,0.287,"Verse"],[6.162,0.487,"five"],[7.05,0.575,"Sattva"],[7.638,0.163,"or"],[7.812,0.525,"goodness"],[8.912,0.5,"Rajas"],[9.425,0.163,"or"],[9.6,0.537,"passion"],[10.55,0.6,"activity"],[11.512,0.15,"and"],[11.675,0.487,"Tamas"],[12.175,0.15,"or"],[12.338,0.55,"ignorance"],[13.238,0.537,"inertia"],[14.512,0.212,"these"],[14.738,0.237,"three"],[14.988,0.475,"modes"],[15.812,0.463,"Ropes"],[16.688,0.5,"Gunas"],[17.25,0.125,"of"],[17.387,0.475,"material"],[17.875,0.45,"Nature"],[18.337,0.537,"Prakriti"],[19.525,0.287,"fetter"],[19.825,0.062,"the"],[19.9,0.45,"eternal"],[20.363,0.55,"individual"],[20.925,0.338,"soul"],[21.275,0.087,"to"],[21.375,0.087,"the"],[21.475,0.425,"body"],[22.413,0.175,"O"],[22.6,0.55,"Arjuna"]]},{"layout":"compare","headline":"Goodness and passion","visual":["Sattva · goodness | Rajas · passion","Pure and illuminating | Intense craving","Binds by happiness and knowledge | Binds by attachment to results","Brings clarity | Brings restlessness and greed"],"L":["L2"],"say":"The mode of goodness, sattva, is pure and full of light, but even it binds, through attachment to happiness and knowledge. The mode of passion, rajas, is intense craving. It is the source of desire, and it binds us through attachment to the fruits of work.","start":48.504,"at":49.08,"end":66.96,"words":[[0.1,0.062,"The"],[0.175,0.263,"mode"],[0.45,0.125,"of"],[0.588,0.525,"goodness"],[1.125,0.625,"sattva"],[2.05,0.225,"is"],[2.288,0.487,"pure"],[2.788,0.125,"and"],[2.925,0.25,"full"],[3.188,0.125,"of"],[3.325,0.375,"light"],[4.112,0.2,"but"],[4.325,0.225,"even"],[4.562,0.138,"it"],[4.713,0.6,"binds"],[5.475,0.225,"through"],[5.713,0.562,"attachment"],[6.287,0.087,"to"],[6.388,0.575,"happiness"],[6.975,0.125,"and"],[7.112,0.588,"knowledge"],[8.088,0.062,"The"],[8.162,0.275,"mode"],[8.45,0.113,"of"],[8.575,0.6,"passion"],[9.363,0.6,"rajas"],[9.988,0.188,"is"],[10.188,0.45,"intense"],[10.65,0.537,"craving"],[11.55,0.15,"It"],[11.713,0.15,"is"],[11.875,0.087,"the"],[11.975,0.4,"source"],[12.387,0.113,"of"],[12.512,0.688,"desire"],[13.625,0.188,"and"],[13.825,0.138,"it"],[13.975,0.375,"binds"],[14.363,0.188,"us"],[14.562,0.225,"through"],[14.8,0.625,"attachment"],[15.438,0.125,"to"],[15.575,0.1,"the"],[15.688,0.338,"fruits"],[16.038,0.125,"of"],[16.175,0.463,"work"]]},{"layout":"story","headline":"And the third: ignorance","visual":["Tamas is born of inertia","It binds by carelessness, laziness and sleep","It deludes the living being"],"L":["L3"],"say":"The third, tamas, ignorance, is born of inertia. It deludes, and it binds us through carelessness, laziness and too much sleep. The three are always competing. Sometimes goodness rises by holding down the other two; sometimes passion does; sometimes ignorance.","start":66.96,"at":67.536,"end":86.976,"words":[[0.062,0.087,"The"],[0.163,0.512,"third"],[0.825,0.575,"tamas"],[1.413,0.588,"ignorance"],[2.025,0.188,"is"],[2.225,0.35,"born"],[2.587,0.125,"of"],[2.725,0.6,"inertia"],[3.688,0.138,"It"],[3.837,0.688,"deludes"],[4.862,0.1